Titanic Survival Prediction using Machine Learning
Project Overview

This project predicts whether a passenger would survive the Titanic disaster based on passenger information such as passenger class, age, sex, family information, fare, and port of embarkation.

The project was developed as part of my Machine Learning learning and practice.

Machine Learning Algorithms

The project uses three classification algorithms:

Logistic Regression
Support Vector Machine (SVM)
K-Nearest Neighbors (KNN)

The predictions from the trained models are displayed through a Streamlit web application.

Dataset

The project uses the Titanic dataset containing passenger information such as:

Passenger class
Age
Sex
Number of siblings/spouses
Number of parents/children
Fare
Port of embarkation
Survival status

The dataset contains 891 passenger records.

Data Preprocessing

The project includes preprocessing steps such as:

Handling missing values
Feature engineering
Creating FamilySize
Creating IsAlone
Encoding categorical variables
Preparing features for machine learning models

The final model input contains 12 features.

